From fb5674a64a78ee27ba48151db802c96922341c9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:35:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dynarmic + PS4: memcpy, memmove and memset run on the host;
 leaf calls followed (up to 4 instructions)

- UserConfig::native_functions (A64 and A32): a block at an address UserCallbacks::NativeFunction
  names (1 memcpy, 2 memmove, 3 memset) is a call into NativeMemcpy/NativeMemmove/NativeMemset with
  X0-X2 (R0-R2), its result to X0 (R0), then a return to X30 (BX LR). New IR ops A64CallNative and
  A32CallNative (side effects; HostCall + the devirtualized callback, as the memory callbacks). The
  function's first 64 bytes are the block's code for the code cache's check.
- Eden (native_functions.h): the addresses from the modules' dynamic symbol tables (defined
  functions; 32-bit also __aeabi_memcpy/memmove and their 4/8 forms, Thumb bit off), read once per
  core at its first translation; plain memory (Memory::GetPlainPointer, new: a page table entry with
  a host pointer) copied and filled directly a page at a time, anything else (GPU-cached, unmapped)
  through ReadBlock/WriteBlock/CopyBlock; overlap with memmove's result. Off with a debugger.
- A64 follow_leaf_calls: the leaf limit five instructions (up to four of the callee's, then RET):
  unity64 unchanged, game64 -2.3%; X30 as a base or source register refuses a leaf too.
- Both on with Auto and Unsafe; off with the boot watcher's extras step, Accurate, Paranoid.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W5pLthrq7391gS4qodPV4u
